{"findings":[{"file":"blackd.py","line":163,"what_goes_wrong":"An empty Python-variant header raises IndexError instead of being rejected as an invalid variant.","trigger":"Send `X-Python-Variant: ` (an empty header value).","expected":"The parser should raise InvalidVariantHeader, so the HTTP handler returns 400.","actual":"It indexes an empty string and raises IndexError, which the handler converts to HTTP 500.","confidence":"high","verified_by_running":true,"reproduction":"import blackd\n\ntry:\n    blackd.parse_python_variant_header(\"\")\nexcept blackd.InvalidVariantHeader:\n    pass\nelse:\n    raise AssertionError(\"empty variant must be rejected\")\n"},{"file":"black.py","line":3621,"what_goes_wrong":"Project-root discovery selects the lexicographically first source rather than their common ancestor, so a nested repository can incorrectly become the root for sibling sources.","trigger":"Format `aaa/one.py` and `zzz/two.py` in an outer repository where `aaa` is itself a nested repository.","expected":"The outer directory, the common project root of both source paths, should be returned.","actual":"The nested `aaa` directory is returned.","confidence":"high","verified_by_running":true,"reproduction":"from pathlib import Path\nfrom tempfile import TemporaryDirectory\nimport black\n\nwith TemporaryDirectory() as temporary:\n    root = Path(temporary)\n    (root / \".git\").mkdir()\n    (root / \"aaa\").mkdir()\n    (root / \"aaa\" / \".git\").mkdir()\n    (root / \"aaa\" / \"one.py\").touch()\n    (root / \"zzz\").mkdir()\n    (root / \"zzz\" / \"two.py\").touch()\n\n    black.find_project_root.cache_clear()\n    result = black.find_project_root(\n        (str(root / \"aaa\" / \"one.py\"), str(root / \"zzz\" / \"two.py\"))\n    )\n    assert result == root\n"},{"file":"black.py","line":554,"what_goes_wrong":"On Windows, parallel formatting crashes when Python cannot determine the CPU count.","trigger":"`os.cpu_count()` returns `None` on Windows.","expected":"Formatting should use the executor's default worker count (or another fallback) and continue.","actual":"`min(None, 61)` raises TypeError before any formatting occurs.","confidence":"high","verified_by_running":true,"reproduction":"import asyncio\nimport black\n\nloop = asyncio.new_event_loop()\nasyncio.set_event_loop(loop)\nblack.os.cpu_count = lambda: None\nblack.reformat_many(set(), True, black.WriteBack.NO, black.Mode(), black.Report())\n"},{"file":"black.py","line":3608,"what_goes_wrong":"find_project_root advertises support for any iterable of paths but crashes for a list because lru_cache requires a hashable argument.","trigger":"Call `find_project_root` with a list, such as `['.']`.","expected":"A list is a valid Iterable[str] and should return the resolved project root.","actual":"The cache wrapper raises TypeError: unhashable type: 'list'.","confidence":"high","verified_by_running":true,"reproduction":"from pathlib import Path\nimport black\n\nassert black.find_project_root([\".\"]) == Path(\".\").resolve()\n"}],"what_examined":"Ran the project suite (119 passed, 1 skipped) and Ruff; traced CLI, HTTP-server, caching, source-discovery, parsing, and parallel-formatting paths, then ran each reproduction above with `.python\\\\python.exe`."}
